# Mutation cases for "a machine hands an algorithm the records and lists it holds and
# takes back what it returns" under the Interpreter (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.15,
# "State an algorithm takes and gives back").
#
# A lowered document calls the algorithm lowered to ecmascript with the variable the
# document holds, and the payload of the event: the Interpreter's records and lists are
# the algorithm's own and an algorithm only reads what it is handed, so nothing is
# converted. `static_state_algorithm` is replayed by `static_datamodel_lowered`, which
# also asserts that it is replayed and not left to a refusal. The mutant takes one
# decision away:
#
#   the algorithm a call names is not the one the document imports.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is reported
# INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_ctest --test-dir build -R '^static_datamodel_lowered$'
mutation_targets sce-build/src/forge/static_js.rs
mutation_oracles tests/integration/AStaticDatamodelRunsLoweredUnderTheInterpreterTest.cpp sce-build/tests/fixtures/static_datamodel/static_state_algorithm.scxml sce-build/tests/fixtures/static_datamodel/scenarios/static_state_algorithm.json

mutation_case "the algorithm a call names is not the one the document imports" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/src/forge/static_js.rs",
     "        self.callee(callee)\n            .expect(\"an algorithm the document imports travels in it\")\n            .call\n    }\n    fn state_list_within",
     "        self.callee(callee)\n            .expect(\"an algorithm the document imports travels in it\")\n            .call\n            .replace(\"ledger_\", \"nothing_\")\n    }\n    fn state_list_within")
PY
